  "structural_change": "PC sr13b (SQ-PCH2 FALLBACK): PD-AUDIT compliant frame (owner must-do 10-21): outline 267.84x300.24 -> 388.8x356.4 um, every face's pins stretched over the full face (N 1547 pins / 386.8 um = 4.0/um, E 1422 / 354.4 = 4.0/um); the 23 SRAM banks in 5 single-memory columns (front x43.2, return x103.68, tag queue x164.16, CDC down x224.64, CDC up x285.12; >=28.5 um std-cell channels) at 38.88 um pitch = 21.6 um gaps (10.8 um placeable rows beyond the 5.4 um halos for the wd_in hold buffers; was 22 abutted 0-um pairs). RTL = sr12g + OT_KVPC_CAL_DNR (calendar data reset-free, -275 RESETN pins), sink CTS 8/20, SRAM-edge guard 2.4/1.2."
 },
 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Pin stages are RTL, not flow: the strap inputs pc__pc / pc__cfg_stack (the 6-11 level input cones of SAFE-AUDIT-KV) land in KEPT pin registers (qkd_static_kv_pc_path_fan_nc_b pc_sr/st_sr + chain station spc/sst, 0 schedule cycles: constant die straps); every chain / boot / HBM word (i_next/i_prev/i_grp/i_grp_h/pc__pi/pc__hes/pc__land_er) is flop-direct (depth 0, kvs_port_domains).  A flow-inserted stage on those would add a cycle to every priced static-join edge age (die_ages.json / kv_static_ages) that the compiled calendar does not have.  KV-PC3 sr6: no waiver left -- pc__fi (fault chain, hck), pc__ki (kc kick word, hck) and x__est__0_1 (embedding boot-ready, ck) land in RTL face registers (fi_q / ki_q / ebr_q, +1 edge each, handed to the die schedule): gate pc_h_sr3 164813 + its sr6-boundary CTS rerun measured those cones at SS -437 / -181 / -168 ps."
 },
